 6. D.C. gunman, victim identified 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A woman walks by with her dog as law enforcement and emergency personnel respond near the scene of a shooting in D.C.'s Logan Circle yesterday. Photo: Ken Cedeno/AFP via Getty Images It took just minutes for a gunman to shoot five people and upend one of D.C.'s busiest neighborhoods yesterday morning, Axios D.C .'s Anna Spiegel writes. 

 What we know: Interim police chief Jeffery W. Carroll identified the suspect as 55-year-old Matt Wade Lambert, an emergency room doctor who lived in the apartment building connected to VIDA Fitness. The man killed was 46-year-old James Stuart, the building's manager and a Northwest D.C. resident, Carroll said. Police believe the shooting was linked to an ongoing dispute between Lambert and his condominium association. Lambert had been fighting the association over alleged leaks and mold, per court records. He filed a lawsuit against the group in March 2025.

 Months later, he told now- Washington Sun reporter Michael Brice-Saddler that he'd spent nearly $200,000 on legal and engineering fees. In those interviews, Lambert said he knew Stuart's daily gym routine. Read on . 

 
 
