 8. 📀 1 for the road: DVD comeback 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 DVD sales and rentals are on the rise after a yearslong decline as more people — especially younger cinephiles — rebuild their physical media libraries, Axios San Antonio's Megan Stringer reports. 

 Case in point: Adult DVD rentals from the San Antonio Public Library have surged 39% since 2022. DVD sales jumped 20% at Half Price Books' San Antonio locations in the most recent fiscal year. "It's the hunt, the find, sharing it — it's all part of the process," says Matt Dalton of Half Price Books.

 "There's a younger generation shopping our stores, and I can see them get excited when they're flipping through the bins or going through the aisles and finding that thing and holding it up. It's pretty exciting." Share this story ... Get Axios San Antonio ... Find your Axios Local city . 

 
 
